1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,217
Now, here's something surprising.

2
00:00:03,647 --> 00:00:07,458
In 1997, Apple was in serious trouble.

3
00:00:07,688 --> 00:00:12,970
Steve Jobs later said the company was about 90 days from going broke.

4
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:15,292
So how did it survive?

5
00:00:23,672 --> 00:00:27,120
To understand that, we need to go back to the beginning.

6
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:34,766
In 1976, Steve Jobs and Steve Wozniak start a small company.

7
00:00:34,896 --> 00:00:36,275
They call it Apple.

8
00:00:38,355 --> 00:00:44,640
But in 1985, after a fight with Apple's board, Jobs is pushed out of his own company.

9
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:48,731
So he starts again. A new company, called NeXT.

10
00:00:50,811 --> 00:00:52,936
Meanwhile, Apple keeps growing.

11
00:00:53,066 --> 00:00:57,496
By 1995, its sales reach $11 billion.

12
00:00:57,826 --> 00:01:01,210
But here's the problem. The company is about to fall.

13
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:07,506
One year later, Apple loses more than $800 million.

14
00:01:07,786 --> 00:01:14,050
It badly needs a modern operating system. So it buys NeXT, for $400 million.

15
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:16,746
And that deal brings Steve Jobs back.

16
00:01:18,826 --> 00:01:25,453
By 1997, Jobs is running Apple again. And his first move surprises everyone.

17
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:29,413
He makes peace with his biggest rival.

18
00:01:29,643 --> 00:01:36,184
Microsoft, up in Redmond, agrees to invest $150 million in Apple.

19
00:01:36,464 --> 00:01:40,680
Jobs announces the deal on stage, at Macworld in Boston.

20
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:45,871
Then he cuts about 70% of Apple's products.

21
00:01:46,051 --> 00:01:48,496
Fewer products. But better ones.

22
00:01:50,576 --> 00:01:53,662
In 1998, the iMac arrives.

23
00:01:53,842 --> 00:01:58,271
And Apple makes its first yearly profit since 1995.

24
00:02:00,351 --> 00:02:04,866
In 2001, the iPod puts 1,000 songs in your pocket.

25
00:02:06,946 --> 00:02:09,732
And in 2007, the iPhone.

26
00:02:09,962 --> 00:02:13,730
That year, Apple earns $3.5 billion.

27
00:02:15,810 --> 00:02:17,786
So what really saved Apple?

28
00:02:18,166 --> 00:02:20,740
Not one product. It was focus.

29
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:26,004
Saying no to almost everything, so the few things that mattered could be great.
